menu "S3Wear UI (ui_framework)"

    choice S3W_LVGL_RENDER_MODE
        prompt "LVGL render mode"
        default S3W_LVGL_RENDER_PARTIAL
        help
            How LVGL renders into memory before the QSPI transfer (P2-04, docs/02 §6).

        config S3W_LVGL_RENDER_PARTIAL
            bool "Partial: two internal DMA buffers of S3W_LVGL_BUF_LINES lines"
            help
                LVGL renders each dirty area in bands into fast internal RAM; one band is
                sent by DMA while the next is rendered.

        config S3W_LVGL_RENDER_DIRECT
            bool "Direct: full frame buffer in PSRAM (measured slower)"
            help
                LVGL renders dirty areas in place into one 410x502 RGB565 frame buffer in
                PSRAM (411 KB). The flush copies (and byte-swaps) dirty rows into two
                internal DMA bounce buffers of S3W_LVGL_BUF_LINES lines.
                Kept for re-measuring with `lcd bench`: in P2-04 it reached 19.9 fps vs
                29.9 fps for partial, because the copy-out cannot overlap rendering.
    endchoice

    config S3W_LVGL_BUF_LINES
        int "Lines per internal DMA buffer"
        range 8 128
        default 40
        help
            Two buffers of 410 x lines x 2 B each live in internal DMA RAM (40 lines =
            2 x 32 KB). 32..48 lines measured the same fps (P2-04); 40 keeps the
            internal heap minimum above budget with the 32 KB instruction cache.
            Partial mode renders into them; direct mode uses them as bounce buffers.
            Free internal heap must stay > 40 KB (docs/02 §6).

endmenu
